 Amazon Announcement
Hello,
Starting January 1, 2027, the United Arab Emirates (UAE) will introduce mandatory electronic invoicing (e-invoicing) for business-to-business and business-to-government transactions.
As Amazon is required to comply with the UAE e-invoicing requirements from Phase 1 (effective January 1, 2027), we will issue Amazon.ae e-invoices for seller fees to businesses that are registered with UAE Ministry of Finance (MoF) accredited UAE Peppol Access Point at the time of invoice issuance.
If your business is not subject to UAE e-invoicing, or you have not yet registered – we will continue to issue your Amazon.ae invoices for seller fees in PDF format, using your account’s tax and legal information.
 To receive compliant Amazon.ae invoices for seller fees, complete the following steps:
1. If you are registered with the UAE- accredited Peppol Access Point, update your Peppol ID in Tax Settings .
2. If you are registered for Value Added Tax (VAT) in the UAE, update your UAE VAT Registration Number in Tax Settings .
3. Ensure your Trade License, Emirates ID, and Passport number are valid in Identity Information .
4. Confirm that your legal name in Identity Information matches your Federal Tax Authority records exactly.
 If your information is incomplete or incorrect, your ability to claim VAT on our invoices may be impacted.
 What is a Peppol ID?
A Peppol ID is a unique digital address registered on the Peppol Network, used to send and receive e-invoices.
 Who is required to register for a Peppol ID?
Any business conducting business-to-business or business-to-government transactions in the UAE is required to register with a MOF accredited UAE Peppol Access Point, in accordance with the implementation phases, and to issue compliant e-invoices for applicable transactions.
 Why does Amazon request a Peppol ID?
A Peppol ID enables the exchange of e-invoices through the UAE e-invoicing network. If your business is subject to UAE e-invoicing requirements, you must update your Peppol ID in Tax Settings to receive Amazon.ae e-invoices for seller fees.
For more information, please refer to UAE Invoicing , UAE Ministry of Finance E-invoicing page and UAE VAT Frequently Asked Questions .
